{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "New Paths"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Family Life"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contents"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative functions for this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Writing about Family"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you are writing about your family, there are a number of items to include. <br><br>First: Introduce yourself. Include your name, age and where you are from. <br><br>Second: Include the rest of your family members (your immediate family, extended family.  Sometimes a person can have a blended family)."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Family Members\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Immediate family\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">mother, father, sister, brother</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Extended family\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">aunt, uncle, cousin</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Blended family\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">half-sisters, half-brothers</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have two half-sisters. This is my father's second marriage."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have a large extended family."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Rhetorical Questions in Writing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Rhetorical questions are questions that you don't answer. You ask rhetorical questions in order to make a point about a situation or to point out something."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Types of Rhetorical Questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Big life questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Aren't we just tiny pieces in a big picture?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Questions that draw attention to something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Do you know what time it is? - meaning it's late</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions to express a bad mood\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What's the point in trying?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions that point to a positive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Didn't  I help you on your last exam?</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structure How + adjective/adverb to ask rhetorical questions. This way, you can ask a question that gets people to think about what you are writing about. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "How much time does it take to become successful?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How much do you really know about your family members?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How well do you really know yourself?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How close are you really to your family?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How crazy are we?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unexpectedly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not expected or planned"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One of my weaknesses is that I am not very flexible.  When situations change unexpectedly, it is a real challenge for me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe family relationships."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "realist"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who accepts and deals with things as they really are"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I consider myself to be a realist.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "face value"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to accept someone or something just as it appears"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I take things at face value "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flexible"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "willing to change or to try different things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One of my weaknesses is that I am not very flexible."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "immediate family"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "close family members including brothers and sister, parents and cousins"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My immediate family includes two older brothers. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blended family"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a family consisting of a couple and their children from this and all previous relationships"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I come from a blended family; this is my father's second marriage. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "half-sister"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sister with whom one has only one parent in common"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are my half sisters, Camilla and Roseanne."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "impulsive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "acting or done without much thought"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Camilla tends to be a little too impulsive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slopes"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "hills for skiing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How impatient is Roseanne going to be on the slopes?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "quick tempered"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "easily made angry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Roseanne is quick tempered."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob08aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interview a partner or friend about their family.  Do they have a small family? Large, extended family? Blended family?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner to describe their personalities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a 75-100 word paragraph about their family."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the paragraph aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I interview a friend or partner about their family."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe people's personalities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph about a family."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my paragraph about a family aloud."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about family life and personal qualities."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask questions about how people are. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about future action, plans and intentions."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Describe your family. How many uncles, aunts, cousins do you have?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do they have different personalities? What are they like?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Writing Spot: Who is Isabelle Richardson?"}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected